  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/969204">Definition <span data-tag="969204">4.4.4.1</span>.</a> Let $\calD $ be a closed monoidal category, and let $\calC $ be a category enriched over $\calD $. We will say that a $\calD $-enriched functor $G: \calC ^{op} \rightarrow \calD $ is <em>representable</em> if there exists an object $C \in \calC $ and a map $\eta : 1_{\calD } \rightarrow G(C)$ such that the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calC }(X,C) \simeq \bHom _{\calC }(X,C) \otimes 1_{\calD } \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }(X,C) \otimes G(C) \rightarrow G(X) \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism, for every object $X \in \calC $. In this case, we will say that $(C,\eta )$ <em>represents</em> the functor $F$. </p>
